\pard\sa40\sb0\fs20\cf3 public.exam_questions where source = \u8216?code_seed\u8217? \u8212? 15 rows, read from the TEST project qeppkiswvclkkwbxmlok.\par
\pard\sa200\sb0\fs20\cf3 Five per science. Every item is Foundation and Higher, and Combined and Triple (tier and pathway are both null on all fifteen). Written by Code for MRB-313 and awaiting your examiner review \u8212? nothing here has been checked by a human yet. Specs: Biology 8461, Chemistry 8462, Physics 8463.\par
\pard\sa240\sb0\fs20\cf3 House style used: a 4-mark item carries four marking points and no levels, because AQA marks those point by point. A 6-mark item is an AQA extended response \u8212? three level descriptors (L1 1\u8211?2, L2 3\u8211?4, L3 5\u8211?6) plus indicative content, with the marking points repeated so a point-by-point marker still has something to hit.\par
